  "notes": "Modified cash basis school district; basis recorded as cash. Governmental funds Total Governmental Funds column used; beginning/ending cash = beginning/ending fund balances (as restated) from p4; ending equals total assets on p5. Statement of net position (p2) used for balance_sheet (no liabilities). Total disbursements printed 6,772,394 is 10,000 below sum of lines (see report_discrepancies; Federal programs reclassification (10,000) on p7, confirmed). Detail is taken from the budget-and-actual schedules for every fund: General (p9-11), Depreciation (p12), Employee Benefit (p13), Special Building (p14), Bond (p15), School Nutrition (p16, object-level breakdown), Qualified Capital Purpose Undertaking (p17), Student Activities (p18). The combining schedules (p6-8) show the same fund amounts and are not repeated, to avoid double counting. Budget-only lines with no 2025 actual are not listed (General: In-lieu-of-taxes 11,000, Other federal categorical grants 50,000; Depreciation capital outlay 403,629; Employee Benefit transfer 12,000 and Reappropriated funds 12,090; Special Building Purchased services 6,194; QCPU Building improvements 1,668). The General Fund Pupil transportation line (323,355) contains a 75,000 transfer to the Depreciation Fund that the p7 reclassifications column eliminates; split into expenditure 248,355 and other financing -75,000 (Depreciation Fund shows +75,000 on p12). Transfers to other funds 55,000 recorded as other financing (matches School Nutrition transfer in 55,000, p16). General Fund expenditure and Depreciation/School Nutrition revenue printed totals include the transfers (includes other financing). State programs/Federal programs lines in the General Fund are reclassified into instruction lines in the p7 total column; recorded as printed. No total printed for Employee Benefit, QCPU or Student Activities disbursement sections; QCPU revenue total 41 is from p8. Student Activities fund shows no total disbursements line on p18 (single line). Re-extracted and re-checked against all pages. Read pages 1-18 of 18 Detail rebuilt 2026-10-27 from the governmental funds statement fund columns (user: statement, not budget schedules): General Fund and Bond Fund columns from the statement (pp3-4; the General Fund column includes the Depreciation and Employee Benefit funds); Other Governmental Funds from the four columns of the nonmajor combining schedule (p8; its Total equals the statement column, with the 55,000 transfer in recorded as other financing). State aid/grants cells split with split_from: General Fund using the General Fund Components State sources (p6), Bond Fund using its budget schedule (p15), so Homestead Exemption, Property Tax Credit and Motor Vehicle Pro-Rate keep their own categories (the top-level State aid/grants line still holds them). Budget-and-actual schedule lines (pp9-18) removed from detail. General Fund printed total disbursements 5,655,591 is 10,000 below its lines (report_discrepancies)."
}
